  "narration": {
    "title": "Baltimore Barges In, Tampa Bay Keeps Climbing",
    "intro": "Milwaukee is still the standard at 85-52, but the interesting motion this week came from below. The Orioles jumped ten spots on a 5-1 run, and the Rays and Guardians kept pushing up while Boston slid.",
    "power_lead": "The Brewers hold first behind a steady 4-2 week, Jackson Chourio hitting three homers and Christian Yelich going 7-for-17. Atlanta sits second after finishing a perfect 6-0 capped by a Chris Sale nine-inning shutout, and Tampa Bay keeps rising to sixth on a 5-1 week and a 1.182 OPS from Junior Caminero. The loudest move is Baltimore, up ten to tenth on a plus-17 week with Gunnar Henderson driving in six, while Boston's 3-4 week and minus-15 run differential dropped the Red Sox three spots to seventh."
  }
